# Container-scan exceptions for security-scan.yml (T20) / T17's Docker
# image hardening. E1 Part 10's own failure-condition language sets the
# precedent this file follows: "CVEs with no fix yet are logged/tracked
# per SECURITY.md §6's patch SLA, not blocking — a permanently-unfixable
# transitive dependency must not make the pipeline permanently red."
# Every entry here must have a concrete reason a fix can't currently be
# adopted (see .github/security/dependency-audit-allowlist.json for the
# same two exceptions, tracked at the dependency-audit layer too) — never
# a bare suppression, and never used to silence a genuinely new finding.

# @opentelemetry/propagator-jaeger — Denial of Service via malformed HTTP
# header decoding. Transitive dependency of @opentelemetry/sdk-trace-node
# (via packages/observability). This codebase only ever registers the
# W3C tracecontext+baggage propagator (packages/observability/src/
# middleware.ts) — the vulnerable code path is never invoked. A real fix
# requires an OpenTelemetry SDK 1.x -> 2.x major-version migration across
# every app/service, out of scope here and risks regressing already-
# verified observability wiring (T11/T16).
CVE-2026-59892

# sharp — inherited libvips vulnerabilities. Next.js 16.2.12 pins sharp
# to exactly ^0.34.5; the fix (0.35.0) falls outside that range. Forcing
# an override risks breaking Next's native image-optimization binary,
# untested. Tracked pending a future Next.js upgrade.
CVE-2026-33327
CVE-2026-33328
CVE-2026-35590
CVE-2026-35591
